      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mount Healthy Heights began in 1817 as a small settlement called Mt. Pleasant before adopting its current name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thirdcenturymounthealthy.squarespace.com/about-mount-healthy"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When Cincinnati faced a cholera outbreak in 1849, residents fled north to Mt. Pleasant, finding refuge in its less crowded streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thirdcenturymounthealthy.squarespace.com/about-mount-healthy"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, many homes in Mt. Pleasant served as shelters for soldiers traveling between Cincinnati and Fort Hamilton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thirdcenturymounthealthy.squarespace.com/about-mount-healthy"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Mount Healthy Heights champions urban agriculture, preserving small‑town charm while encouraging community gardens and local produce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
